                <pb facs="0885" n="757" sameAs="frus:frus1928v01/pg757"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">714.1515/773: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in
                        Honduras</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Summerlin</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-07-27T12:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">July 27,
                                1928—noon</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>67. Your 89, July 25, 12 noon. Paragraph 3 of the Department’s proposal to the
                    Governments of Guatemala and Honduras that the boundary dispute be submitted to
                    the International Central American Tribunal contemplated that the existing Mixed
                    Commission now in recess should reconvene for the purpose of drawing up and
                    signing the necessary arbitral protocol.</p>
                <p>The Department is therefore at a loss to understand the action of the Government
                    of Honduras in completely dissolving its boundary commission and will appreciate
                    a report from you as to the motives which impelled it to take such action.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
